This repository is a snapshot, without history, of the author's working repository (import of the internal
commit 0a7a2de, see SOURCES_IMPORTEES.md; preparation for publication described in docs/PUBLICATION.md).
The reference SU(2) generator su2-heatbath-gpu (Apache-2.0, DOI 10.5281/zenodo.23644087), by the same author,
is the bit-identity reference of the FP64 generator.

The Philox4x32-10 generator is implemented from its published description: J. K. Salmon, M. A. Moraes,
R. O. Dror and D. E. Shaw, "Parallel random numbers: as easy as 1, 2, 3", SC '11 (2011),
doi:10.1145/2063384.2063405. No source code of the Random123 library is included.

crates/kvu/src/cond/numpy_tables.rs contains a literal copy of the normal-distribution ziggurat constants of
NumPy (numpy/random/src/distributions/ziggurat_constants.h, NumPy 2.5.3), distributed under the BSD 3-Clause
license (numpy/random: Copyright (c) 2019 Kevin Sheppard, dual-licensed NCSA / BSD-3, as stated in that file, which
reproduces the license text). crates/kvu/src/cond/numpy_rng.rs re-implements NumPy's SeedSequence, PCG64 and
standard_normal (constants taken from the NumPy sources cited in the file) so as to reproduce NumPy's draws exactly.

Third-party Rust crates used at build time and their licenses: see LICENCES_TIERCES.md.

The code and the documentation were written by AI coding agents under the direction of the author (see AI_USE.md).
